\f4\fs26 It took quite some time to clean up the scientists and give them their first decent meal in several decades, but after only five or so hours they were gathered together, before the High Elvis and his Elvisian Cabinet. Holy Aunt Hayley and Holy Aunt Kathy were seated among the cabinet members, with the Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher either side of the High Elvis. \
\'93What do you have to say for yourself, Mr Treasurer?\'94 The High Elvis raised his eyebrows and stared across the cabinet table at his old friend. Shaking his head he knew nothing would save the Treasurer, the report from the Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher was unequivocal.\
\'93I thought we would have more time. The funds were locked in term deposits and if we withdrew early we would have lost hundreds of thousands.\'94 The Treasurer pleaded, but he knew his fate was sealed.\
\'93I care not for your fiscal responsibility! Your greed has probably cost us everything. What good is money when we are all dead? The time you wasted could have been the time we needed to make the mission a success. Furthermore, your stupidity placed the The Great Teacher, The Blessed Mother and her child in mortal danger. The one-after-the-one could have died!\'94 \
\'93I am so sorry, High Elvis.\'94\
\'93Silence! Your decisions have consequences. You are fired! Now leave the cabinet room.\'94 He stood and quickly headed to the Cabinet room exit, no-one there could even stomach looking to ensure he had left, instead relying on the sound of the door closing behind him.\
\'93Professor Hermann, from what I understand this T-virus operates inside the body in a positive manner? It makes you live a long and healthy life?\'94 The High Elvis did not believe such a thing could exist. Every science book he had brain-dumped told him otherwise.\
\'93The T-virus does much more than that. If you want to know if there is any downside, I haven\'92t found one. I am 62 years old, Mr Elvis, but I am reliably informed I only look 30 and whether or not that is true, I can honestly tell you I feel 20.\'94\
\'93What about these other viruses you have designed?\
\'93I only managed to get two others out of the lab. One acts like a disinfectant. It can be delivered in aerosol or liquid form and it survives and multiplies on surfaces, actively hunting down human pathogens in the open environment. It is non-toxic to plants and animals and leaves a pleasant lemony fresh scent. The only limit I placed upon this organism is that it cannot survive in temperatures over 35 degrees centigrade, it cannot survive inside a human host.\'94\
\'93Self cleaning houses?\'94\
\'93Self cleaning environments.\'94 The Professor knew he was on a winner with that one. A couple of applications per year and an entire house, factory or suburb would be free of human pathogens.\
\'93The Blessed Mother mentioned another virus.\'94\
\'93Yes. I have an anti-virus that inoculates against the T-virus. One shot of this and you are guaranteed a normal life of soul sapping misery.\'94 The Professor happily announced.\
\'93Is Agent Jones still alive? I understand he was not protected by the T-virus.\'94 The High Elvis asked of the Minister for Health.\
\'93Yes. I think he was only suffering from the toxins in the sewage and will be fine. He tells us they will be kidnapping 6 Elvises for testing, very soon.\'94 Keeping updated on the progress of Agent Jones was a priority for The Minister for Health. He was not going to drop the ball like the treasurer. \
\'93If we stop it they will only try again. They must have their tests and they must think they have their killer bio-agent.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley interjected.
